From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:04:20 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 344/344] Meridian: Boost colours follow a drag at once on big live
 apps, the pad as Arc's

On a heavy app (Mattermost-like Time) the colour pad lagged and the page
changed late and only in part: every pointer move re-read the colours of
up to 6000 elements in every tab of the profile and rewrote the whole
paint style; the rest of the page, shadow DOM and the site's own colour
variables were not painted, and live pages were repainted in full every
second.

Each colour the page uses is now read once (a slot) and elements are
marked with it; a pick only rewrites the slots' values as variables. The
site's colour variables (--sidebar-bg, --center-channel-bg, their r,g,b
twins) are set too, open shadow roots get the rules, and elements that
come or change are read a moment later, only they. A tab skips the
script when its boost CSS is the same, and the picked colours no longer
rewrite the boost's style element. On an 18.7k-element fixture: 0.2 ms
of script per drag step (was 62), ~20 ms with style (was 78), no long
tasks while the page changes (were ~55 ms each second).

As Arc's: dark surfaces (a sidebar, a top bar, dark text) take the
second colour (measured on Arc's recordings: L 0.35-0.5, chroma
0.09-0.14), light ones a quiet tint of the main one (L 0.90-0.94, chroma
0.015-0.03, never a bright pastel), accents the main one.
The pad's rim runs magenta at the top, red, yellow, cyan, blue; while
the pointer is on it a faint circle through the main knob and an arc to
the second knob show; the second knob rides that circle and goes round
with the main one. Drags update once a frame. Bigger knobs, a white font
card, Size and Case on orange once changed, labels left and icons right,
and the buttons' icons move (bulb, sliders, no-entry, bolt, braces).

The editor looked washed out whenever the window wasn't the active one
(another app in front, the screenshot tool open): it sits in the
sidebar, which fades to 85% then, so the page showed through it. What
floats over the page (site controls, the Boost editor and its glow) no
longer fades with the sidebar.

